  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^3$ in $(3-4x)(1+x)^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+x)^4&=1+4x+6x^2+4x^3+\\cdots\\\\(3-4x)(1+x)^4&=(3-4x)(1+4x+6x^2+4x^3+\\cdots)\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe contributions to $x^3$ are $3(4x^3)$ and $(-4x)(6x^2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^3&=3(4)+(-4)(6)\\\\&=-12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x$ in $(1+3x+x^2)(1-x)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1-x)^3&=1-3x+3x^2-x^3\\\\(1+3x+x^2)(1-x)^3&=(1+3x+x^2)\\times(1-3x+3x^2-x^3)\\end{align*}$$\nThe contributions to $x$ are $1(-3x)$ and $3x(1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x&=1(-3)+3(1)\\\\&=0\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q16-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^4$ in $(5-2x^3)(1+2x)^5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$380$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+2x)^5&=1+10x+40x^2+80x^3+80x^4+\\cdots\\\\(5-2x^3)(1+2x)^5&=(5-2x^3)\\times(1+10x+40x^2+80x^3+80x^4+\\cdots)\\end{align*}$$\nThe contributions to $x^4$ are $5(80x^4)$ and $(-2x^3)(10x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^4&=5(80)+(-2)(10)\\\\&=400-20\\\\&=380\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "bridge-product-constant-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "180e58d4-d06d-43fd-bbda-9dd23014c20a",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "preserveEmpty": true,
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find the constant term in ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "(1+x)^3\\left(1-\\frac2x\\right)^2",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "8ec2ff48-26d9-4af5-bb0c-f286e6b3233f",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "preserveEmpty": true,
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Write both expansions in full. List all pairs of exponents, one from each expansion, whose sum is zero.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1+3x+3x^2+x^3$; $1-4x^{-1}+4x^{-2}$.\n\n$(0,0), (1,-1), (2,-2)$.\n\nContributions $1,-12,12$; constant term $1$.",
          "worked": "$$(1+x)^3=1+3x+3x^2+x^3,$$\n$$\\left(1-\\frac2x\\right)^2=1-4x^{-1}+4x^{-2}.$$\n\nThe first expansion has powers $0,1,2,3$ and the second $0,-1,-2$. All admissible pairs are $(0,0)$, $(1,-1)$ and $(2,-2)$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}1(1)+3x(-4x^{-1})+3x^2(4x^{-2})&=1-12+12\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q16-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^0$ in $\\left(1-\\frac{x}{3}\\right)^3\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{5}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(1-\\frac{x}{3}\\right)^3&=1-x+\\frac{x^2}{3}-\\frac{x^3}{27}\\\\\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^2&=1+\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{4}{x^2}\\\\\\left(1-\\frac{x}{3}\\right)^3\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^2&=\\left(1-x+\\frac{x^2}{3}-\\frac{x^3}{27}\\right)\\times\\left(1+\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{4}{x^2}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nThe constant contributions are $1(1)$, $(-x)\\left(\\frac{4}{x}\\right)$ and $\\frac{x^2}{3}\\left(\\frac{4}{x^2}\\right)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Coefficient of }x^0&=1(1)+(-1)(4)+\\frac{1}{3}(4)\\\\&=1-4+\\frac{4}{3}\\\\&=-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      }
    ]
  },
